  "worked_solution": "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=t-1.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y={t}^{2}-5.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $-1$ | $-4$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $4$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948638/assets/a9d9be86049e1422d9c5c7e4af24992959637c3771503b13f75865840076149b.png)",
